vkms.patch: two fixes to Debian 6.12.115's vkms, which the VM's image
builds and Linux's master has; dev-log/83-testbed/upstream.md has both faults.

vkms_output.c: let the virtual and writeback encoders clone each other's
crtc, so that a commit may attach the writeback connector to the crtc that
drives the virtual display. Linux 6.12's stable tree, Debian's kernel
among it, checks possible clones in a modeset, which refuses that commit
while vkms leaves possible_clones at each encoder alone.

vkms_composer.c: write each composed row to the writeback buffer at its
own row of the output, not at the row of the plane it was read from,
which differs when the plane is reflected or rotated.

--- a/vkms_output.c
+++ b/vkms_output.c
@@ -105,8 +105,13 @@
 
 	if (vkmsdev->config->writeback) {
 		writeback = vkms_enable_writeback_connector(vkmsdev);
-		if (writeback)
+		if (writeback) {
 			DRM_ERROR("Failed to init writeback connector\n");
+		} else {
+			encoder->possible_clones = drm_encoder_mask(encoder) |
+				drm_encoder_mask(&output->wb_connector.encoder);
+			output->wb_connector.encoder.possible_clones = encoder->possible_clones;
+		}
 	}
 
 	drm_mode_config_reset(dev);
--- a/vkms_composer.c
+++ b/vkms_composer.c
@@ -209,7 +209,7 @@
 		*crc32 = crc32_le(*crc32, (void *)output_buffer->pixels, row_size);
 
 		if (wb)
-			vkms_writeback_row(wb, output_buffer, y_pos);
+			vkms_writeback_row(wb, output_buffer, y);
 	}
 }
 
